from review import card,save,DATE
i='TCS-4495';_,c=card(i);refs=c['references'];refs[0]['locator']='Introduction: independent vertex planting; Hypothesis 1; Section 4.1 and Figure 2: blue region; Section 4.2 and Appendix B: fixed-size recovery.'
refs += [dict(id='gap',title='Detection-Recovery and Detection-Refutation Gaps via Reductions from Planted Clique',authors='Guy Bresler; Tianze Jiang',year=2023,url='https://proceedings.mlr.press/v195/bresler23a.html',pdf_url='https://proceedings.mlr.press/v195/bresler23a/bresler23a.pdf',locator='COLT 2023, PMLR 195:5850–5889. Conjectures 1, 2 and 4; Corollary 11 obtains a gap under secret-leakage planted clique in a dense constant-background regime.'),dict(id='general',title='Recovery of Planted Subgraphs',authors='Wasim Huleihel',year=2026,url='https://proceedings.mlr.press/v336/huleihel26a.html',pdf_url='https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mlresearch/v336/main/assets/huleihel26a/huleihel26a.pdf',locator='COLT 2026, PMLR 336:3488–3592. Introduction and Section 3 treat dense edge probabilities; Theorem 7 is a low-degree polynomial lower bound. The same bound is Theorem 4 in arXiv:2607.00897v1, submitted 1 July 2026, PDF dated 2 July. Both versions checked.')]
save(i,dict(title='Recovery hardness for sparse planted dense subgraphs',formal=r'Assuming the planted-clique hypothesis below, is exact recovery of the planted vertex set impossible in randomized polynomial time throughout the interior of the blue region in the source’s Figure 2? Fix \(0<\alpha<1\), \(c>1\), and \(\max\{\alpha,\frac12+\frac{\alpha}{4}\}<\beta<\frac12+\frac{\alpha}{2}\). With \(p_N=cq_N=\Theta(N^{-\alpha})\) and mean planted size \(K_N=\Theta(N^\beta)\), the proposed obstruction rules out algorithms whose probability of recovering the entire planted set tends to one. This card selects exact recovery and strict interior exponents; critical boundary lines and weaker overlap guarantees are separate targets.',definitions=r'''The graph has labeled vertices [N]={1,…,N}. Include each vertex independently in a hidden set S with probability K_N/N. Conditional on S, draw each unordered edge independently with probability p_N if both endpoints are in S, and q_N otherwise. There are no loops. Thus |S| is binomial with mean K_N, not fixed to K_N. The algorithm sees the entire graph and knows N,K_N,p_N,q_N, but receives no planted vertices or location information. K_N may be taken as a supplied integer; the realized |S| remains hidden.

Exact recovery means outputting a subset Ŝ⊆[N] with Pr[Ŝ=S]→1. Probability averages over S, graph edges and internal algorithmic randomness. Output size is unrestricted because |S| is random. Running time is N^{O(1)} on every input and random tape, with constants allowed to depend on the fixed regime. Parameters have explicit rational encodings of polynomial bit length; the constant-ratio version uses a fixed rational c>1. This is the ordinary finite-input interpretation of the phase diagram.

The Θ notation requires upper and lower positive constant multiples of the stated powers for all sufficiently large N; those constants do not grow with N. Probabilities satisfy 0<q_N<p_N<1. The target concerns every fixed interior exponent pair and its admissible parameter sequences, without demanding uniformity as exponents approach a boundary with N.

The premise is Hypothesis 1 of the source for every fixed γ∈(0,1/2]. In planted-clique detection, the null is G(n,γ). The alternative draws G(n,γ), chooses a uniform k_n-vertex subset, and fills in all missing edges within it. Whenever limsup log(k_n)/log(n)<1/2, every randomized polynomial-time test has liminf of its type-I plus type-II error at least one. No partition or other clue to the clique's location is supplied. This is an average-case detection assumption, not worst-case clique NP-hardness.

Detection merely decides whether planting occurred. A densest-K-subgraph approximation returns a K-vertex set with many edges, which need not be S. Partial or almost-exact recovery permits support mistakes and requires a separate overlap criterion. The fixed-size planting model chooses S uniformly among sets of exactly K_N vertices; Section 4.2 and Appendix B distinguish it from the binomial model. Concentration of |S| around its mean alone does not transfer arbitrary algorithms between them.

The original blue region is max{α,1/2+α/4}≤β≤1/2+α/2. The formal question deliberately keeps its strict interior, avoiding equality cases whose hidden constants and logarithmic factors are not fixed by the caption. It is not asserted equivalent to every boundary or approximate-recovery variant.''',question_type='yes_no',answer_criterion='Establish the conditional obstruction to probability-1−o(1) exact recovery in this independent-vertex planting model throughout the strict interior, or give a polynomial-time exact-recovery algorithm in some such regime with its guarantees proved. Restricted low-degree, spectral or MCMC lower bounds do not establish the all-algorithm claim. Results needing planted-clique side information or a different density or planted-size model must retain those qualifications.',context_blocks=[dict(title='Detection and recovery have different thresholds',text='In the source’s sparse regime, efficient detection is available above β=1/2+α/4, while its cited efficient exact-recovery algorithms require β>1/2+α/2. The blue region lies below the latter and above the earlier hardness or statistical limits.',citation='primary'),dict(title='The caption covers more than one possible output task',text='Figure 2 names recovery, while adjacent text also asks about constant-factor densest-K-subgraph approximation. This card retains recovery and explicitly chooses exact support success in the original binomial planting model.',citation='primary'),dict(title='Later reduction-based gaps have different scope',text='Bresler and Jiang obtain a gap using a stronger planted-clique premise with a known partition and one planted vertex in each part. Corollary 11 uses a dense background and a shrinking probability difference, not the sparse constant-ratio regime here. Their exponent notation therefore cannot be inserted directly into the 2015 diagram.',citation='gap'),dict(title='The 2026 lower bound restricts the algorithm class',text='Huleihel treats general planted structures, with main results for dense probabilities. Theorem 7 rules out sufficiently low-degree polynomial estimators. It is not a lower bound for all randomized polynomial-time recovery algorithms in this sparse model.',citation='general')],why='Separates recognizing the presence of a hidden community from locating all of its vertices. The sparse gap remains a useful test of how computational limits depend on the inference task, even after related reduction and restricted-algorithm results.',progress=[dict(date='2015',text='The source proves planted-clique-based hardness in the smaller red region and leaves recovery hardness in the blue region open.',citation='primary'),dict(date='2023-07',text='COLT 2023 establishes a detection–recovery gap under secret-leakage planted clique for a different, dense background regime.',citation='gap'),dict(date='2026-07',text='COLT 2026 gives results for general planted subgraphs, including low-degree lower bounds, without settling this unrestricted sparse target.',citation='general')],references=refs,status='open',status_note='Read the original model, Hypothesis 1, Figure 2 discussion and fixed-size caveat; checked the COLT 2023 conjectures and Corollary 11 and both COLT/arXiv 2026 models and low-degree theorems. Searches through 12 September 2026 found no resolution of the selected interior under the ordinary planted-clique premise. Exact recovery in the binomial model and strict interior exponents are explicit scope choices from the broader caption.',model_self_contained=True,requires_context=False,review_note='Recovered the blue-region inequalities and specified a conditional exact-recovery proposition. Kept binomial versus fixed size, detection, densest-subgraph approximation and stronger leakage assumptions distinct.',importance=dict(score=c['importance']['score'],method='editorial',reason='A central detection-versus-recovery gap in random graph inference, requiring carefully matched probability models and hardness assumptions. Existing score retained.',assessed_on=DATE),working_summary=dict(sentences=['A random vertex set is planted with a constant-factor increase in its internal edge probability.','The selected question asks for planted-clique-based hardness of exact recovery in the strict interior of the unresolved sparse region.','The source’s detection and recovery algorithmic thresholds differ there.','The planted size is binomial, and finding a dense K-vertex set is a different task.','Later leakage-based reductions and low-degree results checked here do not settle this precise all-algorithm claim.'],basis='saved_sources',source_basis='source-text',written_on=DATE,source_refs=['primary','gap','general'])),notes=['Recovered the original blue-region inequalities and explicitly selected strict interior exponents.','Defined independent-vertex planting, random size, exact support recovery and known parameters.','Stated the source’s ordinary planted-clique premise without adding secret leakage.','Checked COLT 2023 and 2026 results, preserving their different assumptions, regimes and algorithm classes.'],checked_sources=[r['url'] for r in refs]+['https://arxiv.org/abs/2306.17719','https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.00897'])
